From a9babbf7793d073eae4973b9a79e21b77ab5fd72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:15:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 117/119] dynarmic A64: conditional branches on the host's
 flags; constant addresses without the range check

FuseCheckBit: a block ending in CBZ/CBNZ/TBZ/TBNZ (SetCheckBit last, a CheckBit terminal) tests
the register (test r,r / test r32,mask / bt r,n) and the terminal branches on the flags, instead
of setcc, movzx, a store to the stack and a compare with it (half the samples in Bluey's hottest
blocks are in such blocks). FuseCondFlags: a block ending in B.cond after CMP/CMN/SUBS/ADDS/ADCS/
SBCS with only stores of results between: the If terminal branches on the host's flags (Z, N, V as
ARM's, CF as ARM's C after EmitAdd/EmitSub; HI/LS after a cmc) instead of reloading NZCV. Not with
cycle counting (its subtraction comes between). Constant addresses in the fastmem arena (ADRP +
offset: globals): no range check.

Tests: gen11 (every flag setter right before every B.cond; CBZ/TBZ on every bit; edge values),
gen5/6/8 x no fastmem, out-of-arena, mapped arena, no walk: 790 programs the same as the previous
build; cache suites. game.c for AArch64: 3.3% fewer instructions a frame.

